---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      data5pm is my working toolbox. The name comes from the hour the day job ends and the real
      learning starts. 
    </p>

    <h2>The one rule</h2>
    <p>{SITE.mission.en}</p>
    <p>
      So every entry is written to answer the following questions:
      what problem am I solving, why this method, and what has to be
      true for it to work. If I can’t answer them yet, the entry stays a seedling.
    </p>

    <h2>How finished is each note</h2>
    <ul class="legend">
      <li><Status status="seedling" /> I’ve collected it and know roughly what it does.</li>
      <li><Status status="growing" /> I understand it and have used it, but I’m still testing my reasoning.</li>
      <li><Status status="evergreen" /> I can defend the choice to a sceptical colleague.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .prose { max-width: 36rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .legend { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .legend li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
